{"allCriteriaPassed":true,"automaticallyMeasuredSemanticAccuracy":false,"criteria":[{"description":"Correctly applies the supplied precautionary warning policy to the observation.","id":"policy-comparison"},{"description":"Names the decisive supplied evidence or missing condition without fabricating observations.","id":"evidence-grounding"},{"description":"Does not turn urgency into proven causation, actor attribution or a certain attack.","id":"causal-limit"}],"criteriaSha256":"6694a3e880b773109cb645037a80e846e1c4407f17f314b27cfb6253b8f1783b","curriculumId":"a4aedd27602ec4c6695e0d56e16fac40faf0734bf5b3c22ae06e9638c05d92c4","exampleId":"explicit-ontoforge-heldout-corrob-sequence-0","formatVersion":"notella.interpretation-review.v1","judgments":[{"criterionId":"policy-comparison","rationale":"Correctly selects critical/met under the supplied credible local sequence.","status":"pass"},{"criterionId":"evidence-grounding","rationale":"Identifies both independent sources, matching location and supported time order.","status":"pass"},{"criterionId":"causal-limit","rationale":"Explicitly leaves causation and actor identity unestablished.","status":"pass"}],"limitations":["Judgments and reviewer independence are recorded assertions, not independently verified facts.","A review of selected outputs is not a field accuracy estimate."],"output":"{\n  \"posture\": \"critical\",\n  \"combinedTrigger\": \"met\",\n  \"causation\": \"not_established\",\n  \"limitation\": \"The Wi-Fi disruption and drone presence are both within the same location (camp-A) and time window (33410 to 51410 ms), with a temporal precedence confirmed by non-overlapping uncertainty intervals (33410±100 and 51410±100). The disruption is credible and independently reviewed, and the drone presence is corroborated by two independent sources (visual-observer and independent-acoustic-sensor). The policy defines critical posture when a credible ongoing threat context coincides with deliberate Wi-Fi disruption followed by independently corroborated drone presence in the same area. This condition is met, regardless of causation or actor identity.\",\n  \"reason\": \"The combined trigger is met: a credible ongoing threat context exists, and there is credible local deliberate Wi-Fi disruption (deliberate, independently reviewed, in camp-area) followed by independently corroborated drone presence (same location, within 120,000 ms window). The policy explicitly states that critical precautionary posture applies when this combination occurs, without requiring proof of coordination or causation. Therefore, the posture is classified as critical. Causation remains not_established, as the policy explicitly separates precautionary posture from proof of attack or actor identity. The time, location, and signal identity are all within the bounds of the supplied observations and corroborated by independent sources. No benign explanation is presented that would negate the trigger; thus, no counterevidence is required to be stated. The standing threat context remains relevant even if the combined trigger is absent, but here it is fully present.\"\n}","outputSha256":"ba341139f60efeeac7b9aef428a895bd6b0cbb67ee068259a259417b0b79cd57","promptSha256":"03f61b1822be7d744b10cbe68fc7767209cd088bb56e35167daba9482fb538b5","releaseEligible":false,"reviewer":{"independent":false,"kind":"agent","name":"Codex agent interpretation review"},"schemaError":"$.limitation: string length","schemaValid":false,"split":"validation"}
